{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790713288,"nonce":"02ChR+MwrRBcCxiz8ZKcxYqTplw=","message":"Python host construction now has an owned constructor ABI (Zyntax dd2a56f4, Caribou 8de99b4).\n\nThe previous generic foreign-call lowering did not distinguish a constructor's fresh DynamicBox from a borrowed result. In a loop such as `point = Point(...)`, compiled code retained every replaced box. OSR outlining also gave its loop live-in default ownership, losing the release obligation. A 30-million Python→Wren construction run consequently exhausted WrenLift's 4 GiB Immix heap.\n\nThe new fixed-arity generic and all-Float constructor entries return fresh owned boxes. Drop insertion recognizes those entries, loop-carried phi ownership includes owned parameters, replaced unread values die on the back edge, dead shadow phis do not claim the same allocation, and OSR resume parameters inherit ownership. The embedder implements both entries directly over the class constructor.\n\nA 27-million measured-construction stress run now completes without heap exhaustion. With GC state reset before each matrix cell, 3,000,000 iterations and median of nine runs under load about 40 measured Python→Haxe construction at 267.2 ns and Python→Wren at 252.9 ns. The earlier full-row result was 613.6 ns for Python→Wren and included retained objects plus inherited collection debt.\n\nValidation: zyntax_python's foreign integration test checks a 1,000-iteration replacement loop leaves at most the live/final Point boxes; all 388 zyntax_compiler library tests pass.","files":null}]}